# Supabase CLI scratch state. `supabase init` ships this file; it was missing
# here, so .temp/ was committed instead — nine files of per-machine state (the
# linked project ref, a pooler connection string, the CLI and Postgres versions)
# that the CLI rewrites whenever it runs.
#
# The cost was not theoretical: the tree went dirty on its own, which is enough
# for `git pull --rebase` to refuse ("cannot pull with rebase: You have unstaged
# changes"), and two people on different CLI versions conflicted on a file
# neither had edited.
#
# Nothing here is needed to build or deploy. `supabase link` regenerates it.
.branches
.temp

# Secrets. These never belong in the repo.
.env
.env.keys
.env.local
.env.*.local
